<h1>What the page actually did</h1>

<p class="lede">
    Not a description of the problem — the element, the rule that styled
    it, and the browser it happened in.
</p>

<figure class="specimen">
    <figcaption>Every visual report carries this</figcaption>
    <ol class="cascade">
        <li>@layer components</li>
        <li>@media (width &gt; 20rem)</li>
        <li class="is-selector">.caption
            <span class="where">/common/style/exhibition-standard.css</span>
        </li>
    </ol>
</figure>

<h2>Take it with you</h2>

<p>
    Drag this to your bookmarks toolbar, or right-click and choose
    <em>Bookmark link</em>. Pasting a <code>javascript:</code> URL into
    the address bar will not work — browsers strip it.
</p>

<p><a class="bookmarklet" href="#">Debug feedback</a></p>

<details>
    <summary>Copy the URL instead</summary>
    <pre class="bookmarklet-source"></pre>
</details>

<h2>Four kinds of report</h2>

<p>
    The kind sets what gets collected and how you point at the problem.
    Every switch is still yours to change before sending.
</p>

<dl class="railed">
    <dt>Visual</dt>
    <dd>
        The element, the rules that matched it and the layer or media
        query they came from, computed styles, geometry, the
        accessibility check, and the screenshot control. For how the page
        renders: overlap, spacing, colour, a layout that breaks at a
        width.
    </dd>

    <dt>Content</dt>
    <dd>
        Wording, typos, a stale fact. <strong>Select the text first</strong>
        and the picker is skipped: the words are quoted into the message
        and the element holding them is recorded. Sends the element and
        nothing else — computed styles say nothing about a spelling
        mistake.
    </dd>

    <dt>Broken</dt>
    <dd>
        Behaviour rather than appearance: a control that does nothing, an
        image that never arrives, a script that threw. Adds the
        diagnostics — JavaScript errors and failed loads collected since
        the page opened, and whether it overflows sideways.
    </dd>

    <dt>Idea</dt>
    <dd>
        No element, no picker, no capture. The message and the page you
        were on.
    </dd>
</dl>

<h2>Driving it</h2>

<dl class="railed">
    <dt>Picking</dt>
    <dd>
        Click the element. The arrow keys walk the tree — <kbd>↑</kbd>
        parent, <kbd>↓</kbd> first child, <kbd>←</kbd> <kbd>→</kbd>
        siblings — because what you want is usually the container, not
        the leaf the mouse can reach. <kbd>Enter</kbd> locks it,
        <kbd>Esc</kbd> cancels.
    </dd>

    <dt>Sending</dt>
    <dd>
        Each channel is a switch showing its own size, and
        <em>Show exactly what will be sent</em> renders the payload
        first. Form values, password fields and anything marked
        <code>data-debug-feedback-redact</code> never leave the page.
    </dd>

    <dt>Screenshots</dt>
    <dd>
        Captured through the browser's own screen-capture permission, so
        the image is your real rendering. Share <strong>this tab</strong>
        rather than a window or a screen: cropping and the bars over form
        fields only work when the frame maps to the page, and the widget
        says so when it cannot.
    </dd>
</dl>

<h2>Where it works</h2>

<dl class="railed">
    <dt>Accepted from</dt>
    <dd>
        <% if sites.nil? %>
            Any site — no allowlist configured.
        <% else %>
            <% sites.each do |site| %>
                <code><%= site %></code><br>
            <% end %>
        <% end %>
    </dd>

    <dt>Everywhere else</dt>
    <dd>
        The bookmarklet loads on any page, but a report posts to
        <code>/.debug-feedback/report/</code> on that page's own host. On
        a site without the endpoint mounted it fails when you press send,
        with the report already written. Mounting it elsewhere is one
        line in that vhost's config.
    </dd>
</dl>

<h2>State</h2>

<dl class="railed">
    <dt>Reports</dt>
    <dd><a href="<%= mount("/review/") %>"><%= count %> stored</a></dd>

    <dt>Latest</dt>
    <dd><%= latest ? "#{latest["at"]} — #{latest["url"]}" : "Nothing reported yet." %></dd>

    <dt>Store</dt>
    <dd><code><%= store_path %></code></dd>

    <dt>Endpoint</dt>
    <dd><a href="<%= mount("/report/health") %>">health</a></dd>
</dl>

<script>
    /* The app is behind a proxy and is not told its public URL. The
       browser knows it: this page came from it. */
    (function () {
        var src = location.origin + "/common/js/debug-feedback.js";
        var code = "javascript:(function(){var s=document.createElement('script');" +
                   "s.src='" + src + "';document.body.appendChild(s);})();";
        document.querySelector(".bookmarklet").href = code;
        document.querySelector(".bookmarklet-source").textContent = code;
    })();
</script>
